# S3 Worker Kit API Tests
# Use with REST Client extension (e.g., VS Code REST Client)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4006
@bucket = test-bucket

### Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health

###

### Upload Single File (Multipart Form)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/upload/file
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary

----WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="bucket"

{{bucket}}
----WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="key"

rest-client-upload.txt
----WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Hello from REST Client!
This is a test file uploaded via the S3 Worker Kit API.
----WebKitFormBoundary--

###

### Upload Multiple Tasks (JSON)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/upload/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tasks": [
    {
      "bucket": "{{bucket}}",
      "key": "task-file-1.txt",
      "data": "SGVsbG8gZnJvbSByZXN0IGNsaWVudCB0YXNrIDEh"
    },
    {
      "bucket": "{{bucket}}",
      "key": "task-file-2.txt",
      "data": "SGVsbG8gZnJvbSByZXN0IGNsaWVudCB0YXNrIDIh"
    },
    {
      "bucket": "{{bucket}}",
      "key": "task-file-3.txt",
      "data": "SGVsbG8gZnJvbSByZXN0IGNsaWVudCB0YXNrIDMh"
    }
  ]
}

###

### Upload Single Task (JSON)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/upload/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tasks": [
    {
      "bucket": "{{bucket}}",
      "key": "single-task.txt",
      "data": "SGVsbG8gZnJvbSBzaW5nbGUgdGFzayB1cGxvYWQh"
    }
  ]
}

###

### Upload Large File Simulation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/upload/file
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary

----WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="bucket"

{{bucket}}
----WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="key"

large-file.txt
----WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="large.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

This is a larger file content for testing the upload functionality.
It contains multiple lines and demonstrates how the API handles
larger payloads.

Line 1: Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet
Line 2: Consectetur adipiscing elit
Line 3: Sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt
Line 4: Ut labore et dolore magna aliqua
Line 5: Ut enim ad minim veniam

End of file content.
----WebKitFormBoundary--

###

### Upload with Custom Bucket
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/upload/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tasks": [
    {
      "bucket": "custom-bucket",
      "key": "custom-bucket-file.txt",
      "data": "VXBsb2FkZWQgdG8gYSBjdXN0b20gYnVja2V0IQ=="
    }
  ]
}

###

### Upload Binary Data (Base64 encoded image simulation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/upload/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tasks": [
    {
      "bucket": "{{bucket}}",
      "key": "binary-data.dat",
      "data": "iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mNkYPhfDwAChwGA60e6kgAAAABJRU5ErkJggg=="
    }
  ]
}

###

### Test Error Handling - Invalid JSON
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/upload/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "invalid": "json",
  "missing": "tasks array"
}

###

### Test Error Handling - Empty Tasks
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/upload/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tasks": []
}

###

### Test Error Handling - Missing Required Fields
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/upload/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tasks": [
    {
      "key": "missing-bucket.txt",
      "data": "dGVzdA=="
    }
  ]
}

###

# Verification Commands (run these in terminal after uploads)
# aws --endpoint-url=http://localhost:4566 s3 ls s3://test-bucket/
# aws --endpoint-url=http://localhost:4566 s3 cp s3://test-bucket/rest-client-upload.txt -

###

# Setup Instructions:
# 1. Start LocalStack: docker-compose up -d
# 2. Create test bucket: aws --endpoint-url=http://localhost:4566 s3 mb s3://test-bucket
# 3. Start server with LocalStack config:
#    AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=test AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=test AWS_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4566 AWS_REGION=us-east-1 ./worker -mode=server -port=4005
# 4. Run requests above using REST Client extension
